            <ArticleTitle>Herpes simplex virus type I from a patient with radiculoneuropathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>393-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Herpes simplex virus type I was isolated from the CSF of a patient with atypical lumbosacral pain. The features of this case are unusual and important in light of the current understanding of herpes-simplex-virus-associated neurologic disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
